# The configurations hold the commands, sizes and screen indexes of the machine
# they run on, so nothing inside "configs" is tracked, apart from the model.
# The rule is scoped to that folder on purpose: a name based rule would let a
# config named after a project file slip into a commit.
/configs/*
!/configs/_config_model.bash

# Build output of the KWin script is committed on purpose: it is what the
# project loads, and Node.js is not needed to run it.
kwin-script/node_modules/

# Editor settings of whoever is working on it.
/.vscode/

# Backup copies.
*_BAK
*_BAK_*
*.bak
*~

# Earlier revisions, kept locally for reference.
/_GOLD/
/_BAK/
/_TRASH/
